    "result_text": "Confirmed \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line is emitted by `AuditOwnerCreated.java`. It already logged `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipPoints`, and `membershipLevel`. I added `membershipNumber` to it:\n\n- Extended the SLF4J format string and args to include `membershipNumber={}`.\n- Added a private `membershipNumber(Owner)` helper mirroring `OwnerMapper`'s format (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration year, `null` when either the customer code or registration date is absent).\n- Updated the class javadoc.\n\nAll previously-logged fields remain present. The full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` case) passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**, and the emitted line now reads e.g.:\n\n```\nAUDIT - owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-07 membershipPoints=3 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```",
